WEBVTT

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.170
This is Team Rocket’s hideout.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.990
It looks like everyone’s tired themselves out
having fun, and fallen asleep.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.070
Oh, don’t...

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:17.530
“Your skin’s softer than a Numera”?
That’s too much...

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.030
You’re right, though...

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:24.050
Come on!
You’re embarrassing me...

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.190
Oh, that was just Nyarth...

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.090
Tossing and turning...

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:54.880
The occasional jogging exercise
makes for a nice change of pace!

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:04.470
Huh?

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.960
I’ve caught you, Go!

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.740
Ahh! Sorry...

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:11.450
What’s going on?! I can’t see!

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:12.480
Are you okay, Go?

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:04.640
What’s going on? It feels like there’s
something squishy on my face...

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:08.940
Go...
turned into a Gokurin!

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:12.890
Huh? You mean the thing
stuck to my face is a Gokurin?

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:16.230
Y-Yeah. But why would there
be a Gokurin...?

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:21.750
Well, actually, I just saw one
in the bushes here...

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.650
I’ve caught you, Go!

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.120
And then you
ended up like that.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.060
Yeah.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:32.110
Wait, why are you still
holding that pose?

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:35.330
Well, uh...
I can’t pull my hand off it!

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.290
What?!

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.130
It’s stuck tight...

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.450
If you pull harder,
it should come off, right?

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:43.590
I’ll help!

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:51.930
No luck?

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:56.970
Nothing we can do. We’d better go back to
Director Sakuragi’s place and have him look at it.

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:57.950
Right.

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:01.510
What is it, Pikachu?

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:08.450
There’s a Gokurin
stuck to me!

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:09.820
Oh, Satoshi! Be careful!

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:11.040
Make sure you don’t touch it!

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:14.790
Satoshi?

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:17.170
I already touched it!

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:25.210
I wonder why the Gokurin
are sticking to everything.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.390
Yeah...

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:29.950
Well, I’m sure we’ll be fine
once we get back to the Institute.

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:30.910
Yeah...

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.990
Go... You don’t sound happy.

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:38.610
Well yeah, I mean this is just embarrassing,
having you hold my hand like this.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:42.540
What other choice do you have?!
You can’t see with the Gokurin on your head, right?

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:45.010
Well, yeah...

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:45.740
What?

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:46.990
Something’s going on!

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.360
Uh, sorry, what?

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.650
It’s a Houdin, a Houdin!

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:53.330
Let’s go watch!

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.450
What? Wait...!

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:00.960
Gokurin!

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:12.990
What?! What’s going on?!
Why’s everything squishy?!

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.250
Psychokinesis!

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.920
We’re flying!

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:52.760
Director Sakuragi,
please look at this.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.770
What are these readings?

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.130
I’ve never seen life signs
like these before.

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:00.890
Is it a new Pokémon?

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.290
What? What now?

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.730
We’re bouncing,
we’re bouncing!

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.050
Don’t tell me...

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:34.660
Satoshi, you’re not <i>enjoying</i> this,
are you?! Satoshi?

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:38.060
You are, aren’t you?!

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:51.320
We’re spinning...
We’re spinning again!

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:04.170
It’s a Kabigon!

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:10.300
Director Sakuragi,
the energy readings...!

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.210
It’s growing larger than before?!

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:15.800
And this is its predicted route.

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:18.670
It’s heading right for us!

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:24.440
We have footage from the scene
from Renji who went to go shopping.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.820
Bring it up over here!

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:26.560
Right!

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:33.320
What the...?!

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.480
Wasn’t that incredible,
li’l Françoise?

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:45.820
There are more photos of it
being uploaded to the Internet.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:48.090
Try and organize them
into a timeline.

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:50.490
We may be able to
identify the cause.

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:51.840
Roger!

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:59.560
I’ll put the earliest video on screen!

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:03.560
Here it is.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:07.150
Satoshi?! Go?!

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:13.530
Hello?

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.570
Koharu! It’s me! Go!

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:17.160
Go? What is it?

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:18.660
Go!

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:22.050
You have to help us!
We’re rolling around!

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:23.330
Huh?

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.930
Wait, it seems like
we’re <i>flying</i> now!

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:34.230
What are you talking about?
Are you okay, Go?

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:36.660
I’m not!
That’s why I’m calling!

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:37.840
Pass me the phone, Koharu.

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.760
Huh? Sure.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:40.290
Go!

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:41.900
Director Sakuragi!

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:43.970
I believe I understand
the situation now.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:47.960
This was likely caused
by Gokurin’s ability, Sticky Hold!

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:50.480
Huh?! So that explains it.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:52.570
What should we do then?

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:00.620
ieki
Use Gokurin’s Gastro Acid
to release Gokurin’s Sticky Hold.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.620
iei
Huh? Gokurin’s “Yay”?

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.460
No! Gastro Acid!

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:06.140
Their “Yay,” right? Got it!

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.500
No, not their—

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.390
Use “Yay,” Satoshi!

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:12.390
Come on, we need to
command the Gokurin together!

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:13.130
Got it.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.520
Let’s go.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:20.350
Yeah!

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:21.910
One, two...

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:22.640
Gokurin!

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:27.800
Yay!

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.910
I see. So that’s what happened.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:56.190
Still, that let us gather
some valuable data.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:11:01.430
I never knew that Gokurin’s Sticky Hold
comes loose with a “Yay”!

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:05.890
I said “Gastro Acid,”
not “Yay,” though...

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:08.850
Still...

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:10.830
Wasn’t that fun?!

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:13.950
I guess so.

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.280
Yay!

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.130
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:47.810
My head...
My head hurts, meow...

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:56.230
Stop stumbling around
half awake, meow.

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:58.070
I need your help, meow.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:07.900
What? You’ve always wanted
to try cranking this?

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:17.150
If you’re happy now,
hurry up and let me down, meow.

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:24.440
Honestly...

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:29.750
I was having a nice nap.
How did I get stuck in the vending machine, meow?

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:33.260
What’s in that, meow?

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:41.610
Kamukame, meow.

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:44.730
H-Hey, hold on, meow!

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:03.490
Maybe I should’ve asked this <i>before</i> following it all this way,
but where <i>is</i> Kamukame going anyway, meow?

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:14.740
I get it! It wanted to play
in the park, meow!

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:41.130
That’s great, Kamukame.
Looks like Naetle’s going to play with you, meow.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:44.260
Huh? “Don’t make me laugh”?

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.650
“Such notions of kinship
are far from my intent.”

00:13:51.590 --> 00:13:56.390
“Surrender, small one. For you are
a hundred years too early to outrun me”?!

00:13:56.390 --> 00:14:02.070
That Naetle is talking with
the arrogance of a Legendary Pokémon, meow!

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:08.280
“Naetle, you’re the one
who should surrender.”

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:15.040
“Hmph. Those are big words
for such a small shell.”

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:20.000
“Nobody’s getting past me,
whoever they may be!”

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:23.130
Kamukame’s fired up
and ready to go, too, meow!

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:28.460
Could this mean we’re in for a
seriously-real serious battle, meow?!

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:40.350
Kamukame VS Naetle...

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:46.570
Yes, at this very moment, a race of pride
between two Turtle Pokémon is about to begin, meow!

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:50.190
I completely understand
how you feel!

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:53.360
I’ll be sure to watch
your battle, meow!

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:55.970
Sonansu,
you handle the finish line, meow!

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:07.400
This’d make for such a good video.
It’d be a waste to just watch it happen, meow.

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:09.230
Make sure to
record everything, meow.

00:15:09.230 --> 00:15:13.740
Huh? What? Record this?
What a pain.

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:15.870
Stop complaining
and just do it, meow.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:19.000
It’ll go viral when
I put it on a video site, meow.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.690
Ah, whatever.

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:23.820
Now, all the preparations
are done, meow.

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.320
Ready... Go, meow!

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:37.080
Now, which one of them
will reach the goal first?

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:43.830
A Cortoise...

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:49.440
“You think you can have a serious match without me?
Don’t make me laugh.”

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:53.180
It said, barging in, meow.
A Cortoise has joined the race, meow!

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:56.430
Also, hold on. Is it in vogue or something
to go “Don’t make me laugh,” meow?

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:01.070
“Hey, commentating Nyarth,
don’t make me laugh!

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:04.660
“Our race has no need for
your ridiculous commentary!”

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:06.920
What, meow?

00:16:07.780 --> 00:16:10.890
“Don’t make me laugh,
my belly hurts!”?

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:13.990
You mean you literally didn’t want me
to make you laugh?

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.750
That Cortoise was just
really easily amused, meow?!

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:29.090
Kamukame and Naetle have made it out
of Cortoise’s smog, meow!

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:50.110
Naetle rescued Kamukame, meow!

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:04.410
What an upset, meow!

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:09.420
It saved Kamukame,
knowingly putting itself at a disadvantage...

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:12.510
Naetle...
You’re so kind, meow...

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:18.800
“Pay it no mind,” meow.

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:21.770
“I will outpace you before long.”

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:32.820
The next course is a sandpit, meow!

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:36.220
This time,
a Protoga has butted in, meow!

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:42.670
“Expecting to best me in sand is quite risible.
Don’t make me laugh!”

00:17:42.670 --> 00:17:45.790
Seems like “Don’t make me laugh”
really <i>is</i> taking off, meow.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.880
It’s fast!
Protoga’s incredibly fast, meow!

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:58.530
What?
Protoga focused so much on speed,

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:03.220
it forgot to look ahead
and rammed into the edge of the sand pit, meow!

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:06.710
The battle is between Kamukame
and Naetle after all, meow!

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:19.040
What’s wrong, meow?

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:21.650
“Pay it no mind”?

00:18:22.900 --> 00:18:24.950
The leaves on its head!

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:29.440
Naetle, you wouldn’t happen to
be thirsty, would you?

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:33.840
“Nay...” But your leaves
are withering, meow.

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:39.970
It’s insisting it’s
not thirsty, meow.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:54.690
“You...”

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:58.280
“What are you waiting for?
I know you can run.”

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:03.820
“Aiding your foe in battle...
You make me laugh.”

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:05.170
“You’re no foe.”

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:10.120
“We’ve fought our way through this cruel race,
and made it through as comrades!”

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:12.880
“Don’t make me laugh.”

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:16.880
“The real race has yet to begin!”

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:25.010
“Don’t make me laugh.”

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:29.840
Naetle can’t even find any words other than
“Don’t make me laugh,” anymore, meow.

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:37.780
But... But... What a heated race
this has been, meow!

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:42.540
Beating foes that barged in,
overcoming all sorts of obstacles...

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:47.820
These two rivals beyond all others,
spurring each other toward ever further heights...

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:50.190
What a wonderful race!

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:56.670
It’s a massive assembly of
Turtle Pokémon, meow!

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:09.640
Hey, Sonansu!
The finish line can’t go running away, meow!

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:19.150
Hey! Guys!

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:32.010
You’ve played enough for today.
It’s time to head home!

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:41.470
Who is that
Turtle Master-y old guy?

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:47.430
Don’t tell me, they were all
that Turtle Master’s Pokémon, meow?!

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:55.080
I see, I see.
Seems you’ve been having fun.

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:57.510
A fierce turtle race, huh?

00:20:57.510 --> 00:21:00.900
Oh, my, don’t make me laugh!

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:06.820
I get it... “Don’t make me laugh”
was the Turtle Master’s catchphrase, meow.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:18.070
I get it, I get it, meow!

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:20.470
You win, meow!

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:22.760
Goal! ...meow.

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:28.050
“My victory was certain
from the start”?!

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:31.580
“Don’t make me laugh”?

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:34.600
You’ve caught that
catchphrase too, meow.

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:38.120
Yesterday’s foe is today’s ally.

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:42.550
Kamukame has deepened the bonds
between the Turtle Pokémon.

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:51.540
Pikachu!

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:52.410
Utsubot!

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:53.120
Transel!

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:53.920
Lugia!

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:54.710
Achamo!

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:55.500
Morpeko!

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:56.210
Koduck!

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:57.090
Cleffy!

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:57.790
Eevee!

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:58.540
Ishitsubute!

00:21:58.540 --> 00:21:59.210
Teppouo!

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:00.130
Onisuzume!

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:00.840
Metagross!

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:01.880
Subame!

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:02.550
Me...

00:22:02.550 --> 00:22:03.800
Metamon!

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:20.570
Pikachu!

00:22:20.570 --> 00:22:21.400
Usohachi!

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:22.110
Chicorita!

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:22.900
Tamatama!

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:23.650
Mamepato!

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:24.490
Togedemaru!

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:25.240
Lucario!

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:26.030
Odoshishi!

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:26.820
Seadra!

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:27.450
Laplace!

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:28.280
Starmie!

00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:29.080
Miniryu!

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:29.870
Windie!

00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:30.580
Iwark!

00:22:30.580 --> 00:22:31.410
Kucheat!

00:22:31.410 --> 00:22:32.160
Togekiss!

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:32.910
Sleep!

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:33.660
Ptera!

00:22:33.660 --> 00:22:34.500
Raikou!

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:35.250
U'u!

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:36.040
Wooloo!

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:36.830
Ruriri!

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:37.580
Leafia!

00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:38.380
Armorgaw!

00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:39.170
Abagoura!

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:39.960
Latias!

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:40.710
Spear!

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:41.460
Agnome!

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:42.210
Muma!

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:43.300
Madatsubomi!

00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:44.460
Mew!

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:09.560
Now, onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.560 --> 00:23:10.860
Go!

00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:16.370
One morning, upon waking from an odd dream,
I had become a Gorillander.

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:19.400
Wait, Go, you’ve got
a Sarunori on your arm!

00:23:19.400 --> 00:23:22.130
Ooh! How lucky!
Time to catch it!

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:23.500
Huh?

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:25.360
It’s already been caught by someone!

00:23:25.360 --> 00:23:27.920
The person who caught it,
could it be...?

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:31.320
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:34.410
The Lost Sarunori! Who is its Trainer?!
